      "source": [
        "# 🧅 Unit 2 · Module 1 · Notebook 3: The Four Prompt Layers\n",
        "\n",
        "### Find the layers in a real conversation, then build them yourself\n",
        "\n",
        "**What this notebook is about.** People talk about \"the prompt\" as if it were one piece of text. It isn't. What a model reads is built from **four layers**, written by different people at different times: the person typing, the team that built the app, the makers of the harness, and even the model itself. In this notebook you learn to see those layers: first by finding them in a real conversation, then by building each one yourself and watching how it changes the answer.\n",
        "\n",
        "| Layer | Name | Who writes it | Example in a bank's support assistant |\n",
        "|---|---|---|---|\n",
        "| 1 | **User prompt** | the person typing, right now | *\"My card was declined at the ATM, what happened?\"* |\n",
        "| 2 | **User system prompt** | you, the builder of the app | the bank's rules: who the assistant is, what it never says |\n",
        "| 3 | **Harness system prompt** | whoever built the harness | how to use tools, when to ask before acting |\n",
        "| 4 | **Planner prompt** | the model itself, when the harness asks it to plan | *\"1) check withdrawals 2) compare to the limit 3) answer\"* |\n",
        "\n",
        "**The story we follow.** A bank customer had their card declined at an ATM and asks the bank's assistant why. Every exercise uses that message.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Before you start:** do Notebooks 1 and 2 first. This notebook uses the same setup, and the word **harness** (the software around the model) from Notebook 2.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### 🗺️ What You'll Do\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Read a coding agent's conversation** and label every message with its layer, find three harness parts in it, and count its tokens. (Exercise 1)\n",
        "2. **Build layers 1, 2 and 3** on the customer's question and compare the three answers from the same model. (Exercise 2)\n",
        "3. **Watch layer 4 being written:** the model writes a plan, and the plan is put back in front of it as a prompt. (Exercise 3)\n",
        "4. **Sort who wrote what**, and which steps were the model and which were ordinary code. (Exercise 4)\n",
        "\n",
        "No prompt-writing technique is taught here and nothing is scored for quality. Today you only learn to **see** the layers.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### 🧭 How to Use This Notebook\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Task** notebook: fill the blanks (`___`), guided by the numbered `# TODO` comments. **Answer** notebook: the same, already filled in.\n",
        "- Run the cells from top to bottom. Every exercise ends with ✅ / ❌ checks.\n",
        "- Total cost: about **one US cent**."
      ]
    },
