        "id": "2cfe2cc8"
      },
      "source": [
        "# 🔑 Setup: Your OpenRouter Key\n",
        "\n",
        "Same as Notebooks 1 and 2: a secret named `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` in Colab's **🔑 Secrets** panel, with **Notebook access** switched on.\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Model:** `anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5` (1 USD per million tokens in, 5 USD per million tokens out). One line to change.\n",
        "- **This cell also defines `ask(messages)`**, a small helper that sends a list of messages, prints the bill and returns the reply. You built every piece of it in Notebook 1."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "607c4704",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "607c4704"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ==========================================================================\n",
        "# 🔧 Setup: run this cell once, before any exercise\n",
        "# ==========================================================================\n",
        "\n",
        "# ==========================================================================\n",
        "# Step 1: Install the libraries this notebook uses\n",
        "# ==========================================================================\n",
        "# Colab usually has them already; this line only adds what is missing.\n",
        "# - openai: sends requests to OpenRouter\n",
        "# - tiktoken: cuts text into tokens, so we can count what the model reads\n",
        "!pip install -q openai tiktoken\n",
        "\n",
        "# ==========================================================================\n",
        "# Step 2: Import the tools\n",
        "# ==========================================================================\n",
        "import json                         # json: turns Python dictionaries into text and back\n",
        "import requests                     # requests: sends requests over the internet\n",
        "from openai import OpenAI           # OpenAI: the client we use to call models through OpenRouter\n",
        "from google.colab import userdata   # userdata: reads the secrets you saved in Colab's 🔑 panel\n",
        "\n",
        "# ==========================================================================\n",
        "# Step 3: Read your OpenRouter key from Colab Secrets\n",
        "# ==========================================================================\n",
        "# If the secret is missing, we stop with a message that says how to fix it.\n",
        "try:\n",
        "    OPENROUTER_API_KEY = userdata.get(\"OPENROUTER_API_KEY\")\n",
        "except Exception:\n",
        "    raise RuntimeError(\n",
        "        \"❌ No key found. Open the 🔑 Secrets panel on the left, add OPENROUTER_API_KEY, \"\n",
        "        \"switch on 'Notebook access', then run this cell again.\"\n",
        "    ) from None\n",
        "\n",
        "# ==========================================================================\n",
        "# Step 4: Choose the model and look up its price\n",
        "# ==========================================================================\n",
        "# OpenRouter publishes prices per single token; we multiply by 1,000,000 to get USD per million tokens.\n",
        "MODEL = \"anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5\"\n",
        "PRICE_IN, PRICE_OUT = 1.00, 5.00  # fallback prices, in case the lookup below fails\n",
        "try:\n",
        "    for model_info in requests.get(\"https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models\", timeout=30).json()[\"data\"]:\n",
        "        if model_info[\"id\"] == MODEL:\n",
        "            PRICE_IN = float(model_info[\"pricing\"][\"prompt\"]) * 1_000_000\n",
        "            PRICE_OUT = float(model_info[\"pricing\"][\"completion\"]) * 1_000_000\n",
        "except Exception:\n",
        "    print(\"⚠️ Could not look up the price; using the fallback price.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# ==========================================================================\n",
        "# Step 5: Create the client that sends our requests to OpenRouter\n",
        "# ==========================================================================\n",
        "client = OpenAI(base_url=\"https://openrouter.ai/api/v1\", api_key=OPENROUTER_API_KEY)\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# ==========================================================================\n",
        "# Step 6: The bill helper from Notebook 1\n",
        "# ==========================================================================\n",
        "# Turns the token counts of one call into dollars and prints them.\n",
        "def show_bill(usage):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Print tokens in, tokens out and the cost of one call.\"\"\"\n",
        "    if not isinstance(usage, dict):   # the openai library gives an object; turn it into a dictionary\n",
        "        usage = usage.model_dump()\n",
        "    tokens_in, tokens_out = usage[\"prompt_tokens\"], usage[\"completion_tokens\"]\n",
        "    cost = tokens_in * PRICE_IN / 1_000_000 + tokens_out * PRICE_OUT / 1_000_000\n",
        "    print(f\"🧾 Bill: {tokens_in} tokens in · {tokens_out} tokens out · ${cost:.6f}\")\n",
        "    return cost\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# ==========================================================================\n",
        "# Step 7: One helper to send a list of messages and get the reply back\n",
        "# ==========================================================================\n",
        "# temperature=0 makes the answers repeatable, so differences come from the layers, not from chance.\n",
        "def ask(messages, max_tokens=300):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Send the messages to the model at temperature 0. Print the bill. Return (reply text, tokens in).\"\"\"\n",
        "    response = client.chat.completions.create(\n",
        "        model=MODEL, messages=messages, temperature=0, max_tokens=max_tokens\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    show_bill(response.usage)\n",
        "    return response.choices[0].message.content.strip(), response.usage.prompt_tokens\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# ==========================================================================\n",
        "# Step 8: The customer's message, used in every exercise\n",
        "# ==========================================================================\n",
        "CUSTOMER_MESSAGE = \"My card was declined at the ATM, what happened?\"\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"✅ Setup done. Model: {MODEL}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "5191848f",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "5191848f"
      },
      "source": [
        "# 🔎 Topic 1: The Four Prompt Layers, and Who Writes Each One\n",
        "\n",
        "A **transcript** is a conversation written down the way the model sees it: a list of messages in order, each with a **role** (`system`, `user`, `assistant` or `tool`) and its text.\n",
        "\n",
        "Here is the surprise. When you type one line to an AI agent, the model does not read just that line. It reads **the whole transcript**, in order, on every call: the instructions that came with the harness, a project file the team wrote, the line you typed, the plan the model wrote for itself, and every tool result. Most of what steers the model was written by **someone other than you**.\n",
        "\n",
        "To find the layer of any piece of text, ask two questions: ***who wrote this, and how often does it change?*** The line you typed changes every time (layer 1). The app's rules change when the team edits them (layer 2). The harness's rules change only when the harness is updated (layer 3). The plan is written fresh by the model for each job (layer 4).\n",
        "\n",
        "Not everything in a transcript is a prompt layer, though. A **tool result** (what a function returned) and the agent's **final answer** are text too, but nobody wrote them as instructions.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### 🔍 What You'll Learn\n",
        "\n",
        "- To find the **four prompt layers** in a real transcript with the question *\"who wrote this, and how often does it change?\"*\n",
        "- To spot three harness parts in the same transcript (the **six boxes** from Notebook 2): where a **tool** was called, what **memory** was loaded from a file, and where a **check** ran.\n",
        "- To tell prompt layers apart from other text, like tool results and final answers.\n",
        "- To **count tokens**, and see how small your own line is next to everything else.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 🧠 Why This Matters\n",
        "\n",
        "- When an answer is wrong, the fix lives in **one** layer. Changing the wrong layer is the most common waste of time.\n",
        "- Everything in the transcript is tokens, and **all of it is paid for on every call**."
      ]
    },
    {
