      "source": [
        "## 🧪 Exercise 1: Label Each Message in a Transcript With Its Layer\n",
        "\n",
        "In this exercise you read a short, real-looking session with a coding agent: someone typed one line asking for a change to a bank's support bot, and the agent made a plan, read a file and ran the tests. The session is stored as a Python list of six messages (we call them \"bubbles\"). You label each bubble with its prompt layer, find three harness parts in it, and count the tokens of every bubble to see how much of what the model read was written by you.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 🎯 What You'll Do\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Read the six bubbles printed by the cell.\n",
        "2. For each bubble, write its **layer**: `1`, `2`, `3`, `4`, or `0` if it is not a prompt layer (a tool result, or the agent's final answer).\n",
        "3. Answer three questions: which bubble shows a **tool** being called, which one is **memory** loaded from a file, and which one proves a **check** ran.\n",
        "4. Count the tokens in each bubble and see what share of the whole is the line you typed.\n",
        "\n",
        "👉 By the end, you'll be able to look at any transcript and say who wrote each part, and how small the part you typed really is.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### ✅ You Succeed When\n",
        "\n",
        "- All 6 layer labels and all 3 box answers get a ✅.\n",
        "- Your typed line is **13 tokens**.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### 🛠 Technical Info\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Hint for layers:** the harness's makers wrote the general rules for any coding job; the team wrote the project file (`CLAUDE.md`, a file the agent reads at the start of every session); you typed the request; the model wrote the plan.\n",
        "- **Tokenizer:** `tiktoken` with `o200k_base`, the same one as in Notebook 1.\n",
        "- The transcript is shortened to fit on screen. Real harness instructions are thousands of words long.\n",
        "- No API call in this exercise, so it costs nothing.\n",
        "- **Difficulty:** 🟢 Level 1, Guided\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### 🚀 Level Up (optional)\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Add a seventh bubble with a long tool result (paste 30 lines of any code as its text). What happens to your share of the tokens?\n",
        "2. Which bubbles would change if the same agent worked on a different project? Which would stay the same? Write one sentence on why."
      ]
