      "source": [
        "## 🧪 Exercise 2: Send the Same Question With 1, 2 and 3 Layers\n",
        "\n",
        "In this exercise you send the customer's question to the same model three times. The first time it gets only the question. The second time it also gets your bank's rules, which you write yourself. The third time, a harness's rules sit on top of yours. Then you compare the three answers side by side. This shows that the answer depends on all the text in front of the question, and that every layer you add costs tokens on every call.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 🎯 What You'll Do\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Version A (layer 1):** send only the customer's message.\n",
        "2. **Version B (layers 2 + 1):** write `BANK_RULES`, your user system prompt, in **two or three sentences**: who the assistant is, and what it may and may not say. Send it as a system message in front of the customer's message.\n",
        "3. **Version C (layers 3 + 2 + 1):** put the coding agent's rules in front of your rules, and send again.\n",
        "4. Compare the three answers and the tokens each one read.\n",
        "\n",
        "👉 By the end, you'll see one model give three different answers, and the only reason is the text you put in front of the question.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### ✅ You Succeed When\n",
        "\n",
        "- `BANK_RULES` has 2 or 3 sentences.\n",
        "- The tokens in grow from A to B to C (each layer is paid for).\n",
        "- You can see in the printed answers that B sounds like a bank's assistant, and C is pulled toward a coding agent's job.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### 🛠 Technical Info\n",
        "\n",
        "- **A system message:** `{\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": \"...\"}`, placed **before** the user message.\n",
        "- **Joining layers 3 and 2:** `HARNESS_RULES + \"\\n\\n\" + BANK_RULES` (the harness's rules come first, as in a real harness; `\"\\n\\n\"` adds a blank line between them).\n",
        "- **Temperature 0** for all three calls, so the differences come from the layers and not from randomness.\n",
        "- **Difficulty:** 🟡 Level 2, Scaffolded (you write a real prompt)\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### 🚀 Level Up (optional)\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Write a **bank** harness instead: replace `HARNESS_RULES` with three sentences a bank assistant's harness would ship with (for example, how to answer when it has no account data). Does version C now help the customer instead of confusing the model?\n",
        "2. Add *\"Answer in Spanish.\"* to `BANK_RULES`. Which layer did you just change, and who would normally change it?"
      ]
    },
