      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "39cccb4a",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "39cccb4a"
      },
      "source": [
        "# 📝 Topic 3: The Planner Prompt, a Plan the Model Writes for Itself\n",
        "\n",
        "The fourth layer is the strangest one: a prompt **the model writes for itself**.\n",
        "\n",
        "It works like this. The harness asks the model to **write a plan before acting**. The model writes something like *\"1) find the reason 2) check the limit 3) answer kindly\"*. Then the harness puts that plan **back in front of the model** on the next call. Now the plan is text the model reads, so it is a prompt too: one the model wrote.\n",
        "\n",
        "For a short chat you rarely see this layer. For agents that work through many steps (like the coding agent in Exercise 1, or a system that runs for hours), it is essential: the plan keeps the agent on track.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### 🔍 What You'll Learn\n",
        "\n",
        "- The **planner prompt**: the model's own plan, used as a prompt on the next call.\n",
        "- Who does what: the **harness asks** for a plan and **puts it back**; the **model writes** it.\n",
        "- In code, the plan is just one more message in the list, with the role `\"assistant\"` (the role for text the model wrote).\n",
        "\n",
        "### 🧠 Why This Matters\n",
        "\n",
        "- Long-running agents live on their plans. When an agent goes off track, reading its plan is often how you find out why.\n",
        "- It shows again that \"the prompt\" is put together by software, from pieces written by different authors."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "f429fc95",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "f429fc95"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 🧪 Exercise 3: Ask the Model for a Plan, Then Feed It Back\n",
        "\n",
        "In this exercise you watch layer 4 being made. In the first call, the harness asks the model to write only a short plan for answering the customer, without answering yet. In the second call, the harness puts that plan back into the list of messages and asks the model to follow it. You then print everything the model read in the second call, with each message's layer, so you can see the plan sitting there as a prompt.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 🎯 What You'll Do\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Call 1:** ask the model to write only a short numbered plan for answering the customer.\n",
        "2. Print the plan: this is the prompt the agent writes to itself.\n",
        "3. **Call 2:** put the plan back into the list of messages, ask the model to follow it, and print the answer.\n",
        "4. Print the messages of call 2 with their layer numbers.\n",
        "\n",
        "👉 By the end, you'll have seen a model write its own prompt, and the harness use it.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### ✅ You Succeed When\n",
        "\n",
        "- The plan has at least 2 numbered steps.\n",
        "- The plan is inside the messages of call 2, as an `\"assistant\"` message.\n",
        "- You see the final answer for the customer.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### 🛠 Technical Info\n",
        "\n",
        "- **The harness's request for a plan** is one more sentence in the system message: `PLANNER_REQUEST`.\n",
        "- **Putting the plan back:** `{\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": plan}`, then a short user message from the harness: *\"Now follow your plan and write the reply to the customer.\"*\n",
        "- **Counting numbered steps:** `re.findall(r\"^\\s*\\d+[.)]\", plan, re.MULTILINE)` finds lines that start with `1.` or `1)`.\n",
        "- **Difficulty:** 🟡 Level 2, Scaffolded\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### 🚀 Level Up (optional)\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Edit the plan by hand before call 2 (for example, add a step *\"4) Offer to raise the daily limit for an upcoming trip\"*) and run only Steps 3 to 5 again. Does the answer follow **your** edited plan? You just changed layer 4 yourself, which is what people do when they review an agent's plan before it acts.\n",
        "2. Remove the plan message from call 2. Is the answer different? Better or worse?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "90a26ad2",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "90a26ad2"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ==========================================================================\n",
        "# 📝 Exercise 3: Ask the Model for a Plan, Then Feed It Back\n",
        "# ==========================================================================\n",
        "\n",
        "# Make sure the Setup cell ran first (it creates ask() and CUSTOMER_MESSAGE)\n",
        "assert \"ask\" in globals(), \"Run the Setup cell at the top of the notebook first.\"\n",
        "\n",
        "import re         # re: to find the numbered steps of the plan\n",
        "import textwrap   # textwrap: wraps long lines so the answer is easy to read\n",
        "\n",
        "# Your user system prompt (layer 2). If you wrote BANK_RULES in Exercise 2, we reuse it;\n",
        "# if you skipped Exercise 2, we use a ready-made one.\n",
        "if \"BANK_RULES\" not in globals() or not isinstance(BANK_RULES, str):\n",
        "    BANK_RULES = (\n",
        "        \"You are a bank's support assistant: be brief, kind and plain-spoken. \"\n",
        "        \"You cannot see accounts, so explain the usual reasons and offer to connect the customer to a person. \"\n",
        "        \"Never ask for or show a full card number.\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "# ==========================================================================\n",
        "# Step 1: The harness asks for a plan\n",
        "# ==========================================================================\n",
        "# This sentence is written by the harness, so it is layer 3.\n",
        "PLANNER_REQUEST = (\n",
        "    \"Before answering, write ONLY a short numbered plan (3 steps at most) of how you will answer \"\n",
        "    \"this customer. Do not answer yet.\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# ==========================================================================\n",
        "# Step 2: Call 1. The model writes its plan\n",
        "# ==========================================================================\n",
        "plan_messages = [\n",
        "    {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": BANK_RULES + \"\\n\\n\" + PLANNER_REQUEST},   # layers 2 + 3\n",
        "    {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": CUSTOMER_MESSAGE},                             # layer 1\n",
        "]\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 70)\n",
        "print(\"📝 CALL 1: THE MODEL WRITES ITS PLAN\")\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 70)\n",
        "# ask() returns two things: the reply and the token count. \"_\" is a name for a value we don't need.\n",
        "# TODO 1: Send plan_messages with the ask() helper; keep the reply as `plan` (ignore the token count with _)\n",
        "plan, _ = ask(___)  # <-- Fill in the blank\n",
        "print(plan)\n",
        "\n",
        "# ==========================================================================\n",
        "# Step 3: Call 2. The harness puts the plan back in front of the model\n",
        "# ==========================================================================\n",
        "# The plan goes back as an \"assistant\" message, because the model wrote it.\n",
        "# Then the harness adds one short instruction: follow your plan.\n",
        "answer_messages = [\n",
        "    {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": BANK_RULES},                                          # layer 2\n",
        "    {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": CUSTOMER_MESSAGE},                                         # layer 1\n",
        "    # TODO 2: Put the plan back as a message written by the model (role \"assistant\")\n",
        "    {\"role\": ___, \"content\": ___},  # <-- Fill in the blanks (layer 4)\n",
        "    {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Now follow your plan and write the reply to the customer.\"},  # from the harness\n",
        "]\n",
        "print()\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 70)\n",
        "print(\"💬 CALL 2: THE MODEL FOLLOWS ITS OWN PLAN\")\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 70)\n",
        "final_answer, _ = ask(answer_messages)\n",
        "print(textwrap.fill(final_answer, width=100))\n",
        "\n",
        "# ==========================================================================\n",
        "# Step 4: Show what the model read on call 2, with the layer of each message\n",
        "# ==========================================================================\n",
        "# This is \"the prompt\" of call 2: put together by software, from four different authors.\n",
        "LAYER_OF = {0: \"layer 2 · user system prompt\", 1: \"layer 1 · user prompt\",\n",
        "            2: \"layer 4 · planner prompt (written by the model)\", 3: \"from the harness\"}\n",
        "print()\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 70)\n",
        "print(\"🧅 WHAT THE MODEL READ ON CALL 2\")\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 70)\n",
        "# enumerate gives each message's position (0, 1, 2, 3), which we use to look up its layer\n",
        "for position, message in enumerate(answer_messages):\n",
        "    preview = message[\"content\"].replace(\"\\n\", \" \")[:80]   # the first 80 characters, on one line\n",
        "    print(f\"{message['role']:<9} [{LAYER_OF[position]}]\\n          {preview}...\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# ==========================================================================\n",
        "# Step 5: Self-check\n",
        "# ==========================================================================\n",
        "# The pattern finds lines that start with a number followed by \".\" or \")\", like \"1.\" or \"2)\".\n",
        "# re.MULTILINE makes ^ mean \"the start of any line\", not only the start of the text.\n",
        "# TODO 3: Find the numbered steps in the plan (see Technical Info for the pattern)\n",
        "numbered_steps = re.findall(___, plan, re.MULTILINE)  # <-- Fill in the blank\n",
        "print()\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 70)\n",
        "print(\"✅ SELF-CHECK\")\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 70)\n",
        "print(f\"{'✅' if len(numbered_steps) >= 2 else '❌'} The plan has {len(numbered_steps)} numbered steps (2 or more wanted)\")\n",
        "plan_is_read = any(m[\"role\"] == \"assistant\" and m[\"content\"] == plan for m in answer_messages)   # any(): True if at least one message matches\n",
        "print(\"✅ The plan is in call 2's messages, as an assistant message\" if plan_is_read else \"❌ The plan is not in call 2's messages\")\n",
        "print(\"✅ The customer got an answer\" if final_answer else \"❌ No final answer\")\n",
        "print()\n",
        "print(\"🧠 The harness ASKED for a plan and PUT IT BACK. The model WROTE it. Software put the prompt together.\")"
      ]
    },
